    "complete_local_proof": "For primitive r=(x,y), reflection integrality gives (q(r))|2I(r), I(r)=(theta*x,(y,S23)). The coefficient theta is a unit and S23 has Smith invariants 1^22,3. Away from the inert primes (2),(3), local unimodularity and primitivity force v(q)=0. At (2), I(r) is a unit and v_2(q)<=v_2(2)=1. At (3), q-divisibility forces x divisible by 3 and y into the one-dimensional pairing radical; its primitive pairing ideal has valuation exactly one, so v_3(q)<=1. The Minkowski bound 14/9 gives class number one, and -1, theta, theta^2-2 have full unit-signature rank, so totally positive units are squares. The complete canonical norms are therefore 1,2,3,6. For norms 3 and 6 every coefficient of y lies in the mod-three pairing radical.",
    "norm_3_and_6_spatial_gate": "each of u,v,w lies in the mod-three pairing radical"
